{
  "formTitle": "MC-410 Disability Accommodation Request",
  "_comment": "MC-410 is CONFIDENTIAL and is not filed in the case file: it goes to the court's ADA coordinator, not into the record the other side can read (Cal. Rules of Court, rule 1.100; the form prints CONFIDENTIAL under its number). It comes into the packet when the filer says they need an accommodation for a disability at court. Page 1 is the filer's; page 2 says 'Court fills out below' and every field under it - the court's contact line, granted or denied, the reasons, the dates it covers and the signature - is marked courtUse. The case number is courtUse as on every form in the packet. The filer's own details carry the packet's names (person_asking_protection_*, court_name_and_street_address) so they are asked once. Names come from the printed labels and the rectangles: the XFA path for the accommodation box is List4[0].LI1[0].Medical-Condition[0] and for the helper's name SignSub[0].Name[0], neither of which says what the box is. The eight push buttons (print, save, clear, three links and the footer link) are type button and courtUse; the sanitizer drops them and draws the caption of any that was printing words.",
